  "id": "voluntary-attention",
  "term": "voluntary attention",
  "definition": "Voluntary attention is the deliberate ability to direct and hold one’s mental activity on a chosen object or line of thought. In this historical source, a deficiency of voluntary attention means reduced power to concentrate intentionally in a desired direction.",
